From a68336e207e6eb33eb7503101c62e91377ed4448 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:45:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08532/11362] Land early-stop-grace counterfactual A/B, ship
 grace=1300 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6220)

exp6214: replays the exact recorded level_up_actions sequences from
results/early_stop_sweep_20260726/rows_*.json (null-grace rows, so
nothing was ever truncated) against candidate grace values, across all
25 public games x 3 seeds (75 rows) at the shipped MAX_ACTIONS=2000
budget. This is an EXACT counterfactual, not an approximation -- the
grace mechanism (is_done(), arc_competition_agent.py:4439-4449) cannot
change agent behavior before the moment it fires, so a run recorded with
grace off already contains the ground truth needed to compute what any
candidate value would have done. adversarial_verify.py: 0 flags.

Result: grace=400 and grace=800 both cost 4 of the baseline's 40 total
levels (cd82, tu93 -- confirming the earlier chat-audit finding at full
25-game scale) while saving 17,435-28,937 actions. The largest value
that costs ZERO levels against this data is 1204 -- but that is exactly
tu93's measured gap, a fit to the observed sample rather than a
safety-margined threshold. 1300 gives the same zero-level-cost guarantee
with a 96-action margin, saving ~4,753 of 145,614 total actions (~3.3%).
Operator directive: ship 1300, choosing margin over the sample-fit value.

The honest bottom line, recorded in REQ-ARC-WMTE-6220's spec entry: a
genuinely safe grace value does not buy much here -- ~3.3%, not the
~20% the original (wrong) "no score cost" framing implied.

SUBMITTED_EARLY_STOP_GRACE: None -> 1300. Third dated correction comment
on this constant this session (first: the wiring was dead; second: the
"no score cost" premise was false; third: this A/B's actual number).

11 results/*.json artifacts get a freshness_acknowledgements entry:
every one was generated under a prior value (off, or 400 for the brief
window it shipped), never under 1300, so this affects future runs only.
One second-order cascade resolved the same way.

